# SoftMedia Specific
# Anchored to the repo root (leading slash): these ignore the TOP-LEVEL runtime media/data
# folders ONLY. Without the leading slash, "media/" and "data/" also matched SOURCE directories
# named Media/Data (e.g. src/SoftMedia.Server/Services/Media, src/SoftMedia.Server/Data) —
# case-insensitively on Windows — silently hiding source files. The unanchored "data/" rule had
# excluded AppDbContext.cs / AppDbContextFactory.cs / DbInitializer.cs from git entirely.
/media/
/data/
# Runtime artifacts that live alongside the now-tracked Data-layer source.
/src/SoftMedia.Server/Data/backups/
/src/SoftMedia.Server/Data/task-status.json
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
transcode-temp/
**/cache/
**/wwwroot/cache/
test-fixtures/

# Test / build output noise (never commit; see Phase 2 / E1 of the hardening plan)
**/build*.log
**/build_*.txt
**/test_log*.txt
**/test_run_*.txt
**/test_build_*.txt
**/errors.log

# Vendored ffmpeg removed from git (see docs/plans/licensing-and-repo-hygiene-plan-2026-06-18.md).
# jellyfin-ffmpeg is fetched at setup time, not committed. These rules prevent re-vendoring.
/src/SoftMedia.Server/ffmpeg-bin/
/src/SoftMedia.Server/ffmpeg.exe.bak
/src/SoftMedia.Server/ffprobe.exe.bak
*.exe.bak
